// Scratch additions to `packages/stdlib/@tao/Prelude.tao`; they graduate there at absorption.

// A unit family (Decisions §2). A value of a family carries its family and normalizes to the
// family's base; `.unit` on a number constructs one and `.unit` on a value reads it back as a number
// in that unit. Families, units, and ratios are a table the compiler and runtime share — registering a
// family adds a row, not a language construct. This tranche registers `duration` only:
//
//   duration   base ns   ms · s · min · h · d · wk, and the long singular/plural aliases
//              (`1.second`, `30.seconds`, `10.minutes`, …); there is no bare `m` — `m` is meters
//
// Readings beyond the units: `.Clock` renders a duration as clock text — whole seconds, `m:ss`
// under an hour, `h:mm:ss` from an hour up, `0:00` for zero or negative.
primitive duration
